From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TactiQ OS BSP <bsp@tactiqedge.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 21:03:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] boot: fit: refuse a configuration below a rollback floor held
 in the TPM

A FIT signature tells U-Boot who signed an image, not when: an older
configuration signed with the same key verifies as well as the current
one, so writing an older boot and root slot, or pointing BOOT_ORDER at the
slot that holds one, rolls the device back.

Add CONFIG_FIT_ROLLBACK_TPM. After the configuration signature verifies,
fit_image_load() reads the configuration's u32 "rollback-index" (0 when
absent), once per bootm on the kernel load, and refuses the configuration
when the index is below a floor kept in a TPM NV bit field. The node is
signed with the configuration, so the index cannot be changed without
breaking the signature.

The floor N is the N lowest bits set; the TPM only sets bits, so the floor
cannot go down, and the field holds 64 levels. A counter would not do: its
first increment starts it at the highest value any counter on the TPM has
held. The index is defined under the platform hierarchy with
bits|ppwrite|ppread|authread|platformcreate: written only with platform
authorization, which the OS never holds once the platform hierarchy is
disabled before handover (CONFIG_MEASURED_BOOT_LOCK_PLATFORM), and read
with its own empty authorization. U-Boot defines it when it is absent and
refuses to boot when an index with any other attribute set or size is at
the same handle.

The floor is raised only to the index of the configuration just verified,
only when the environment variable fit_rollback_raise is 1 (the boot
script sets it for a slot the OS has confirmed), and only when this
bootloader has booted the same configuration from the same slot before.
The last configuration booted from each slot is recorded, as the SHA-256
of its signature values, in fit_seen_A or fit_seen_B. A confirmed counter
alone is not enough: a system that predates this change installs a slot
with the counter of a confirmed one, and raising the floor on the first
boot of such a slot leaves no slot to fall back to if it then fails. With
the record, a slot written by anyone raises the floor only after it has
booted once and the OS has confirmed it. Any TPM failure refuses the
configuration.
---
 boot/Kconfig        |  37 +++++++
 boot/Makefile       |   1 +
 boot/fit-rollback.c | 247 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 boot/image-fit.c    |  10 ++
 include/image.h     |  17 +++
 5 files changed, 312 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 boot/fit-rollback.c

diff --git a/boot/Kconfig b/boot/Kconfig
index 910d892b..cc51b247 100644
--- a/boot/Kconfig
+++ b/boot/Kconfig
@@ -147,6 +147,43 @@ config FIT_SIGNATURE_MAX_SIZE
 	  device memory. Assure this size does not extend past expected storage
 	  space.
 
+config FIT_ROLLBACK_TPM
+	bool "Refuse FIT configurations below a rollback floor held in the TPM"
+	depends on FIT_SIGNATURE && TPM_V2
+	help
+	  Read the u32 "rollback-index" property of the FIT configuration
+	  being booted (0 when absent) and refuse the configuration when the
+	  index is below a floor kept in a TPM NV bit field. Floor N is
+	  stored as the N lowest bits set, so the TPM itself keeps it from
+	  going down; the field holds 64 levels.
+
+	  The index is defined under the platform hierarchy, written only
+	  with platform authorization and read with its own empty
+	  authorization. Platform authorization exists only until the
+	  platform hierarchy is disabled before the OS starts
+	  (MEASURED_BOOT_LOCK_PLATFORM), so the OS can read the floor but
+	  cannot raise, lower or delete it. The bootloader defines the
+	  index when it is absent and refuses to boot when an index with
+	  other attributes sits at the same handle.
+
+	  The floor is raised only to the index of a configuration whose
+	  signature has just been verified, only when the environment
+	  variable "fit_rollback_raise" is "1" (the boot script sets it for a
+	  slot that the OS has confirmed), and only when the same
+	  configuration was booted from the same slot before. The last
+	  configuration booted from each slot is recorded in "fit_seen_A" or
+	  "fit_seen_B" (the slot is "rauc_slot"); both must be importable
+	  from the saved environment (ENV_FLAGS_LIST_STATIC). Any TPM failure
+	  refuses the boot.
+
+config FIT_ROLLBACK_TPM_NV_INDEX
+	hex "TPM NV index of the FIT rollback floor"
+	depends on FIT_ROLLBACK_TPM
+	default 0x500018
+	help
+	  NV index of the floor, without the NV handle type byte (0x500018
+	  is handle 0x01500018).
+
 config FIT_CIPHER
 	bool "Enable ciphering data in a FIT uImages"
 	depends on DM
